ng fast — so eviction doesn't obviously explain an empty capture. Measuring the actual cause rather than guessing:
Proven: line-count marking is unsound on a **byte-bounded** ring buffer — long SCST lines evict a greater *number* of shorter old lines, so the total count can fall below the mark and `tail -n +N` yields nothing. Replacing it with a self-identifying kmsg token:
